# The build context used to be the whole project directory, so `COPY . .` put
# three things into every image that had no business being there:
#
#   - node_modules from the host (139 MB), which the RUN below then installed
#     again on top: the same tree stored twice, in two layers
#   - data/, which is MOUNTED at runtime (./data:/data in docker-compose.yml),
#     so the copy at /app/data was never read by anything — it was a frozen
#     snapshot of db.sqlite, of filters.json with the private patterns, and of
#     every filters.json.bak-* and db-backup-* ever left in there
#   - .env, carrying TUNNEL_TOKEN and the admin password hash
#
# The .env one was not merely untidy. src/index.ts calls dotenv.config(), which
# does not override a variable already set — but DOES fill a gap. So a variable
# deleted from the host .env in order to switch something off was silently
# restored from the copy baked into the image at build time. Verified rather
# than assumed: a container handed no FEEDGEN_ADMIN_UI at all still logged
# "admin: UI mounted at /admin on the public app", using the password hash
# frozen in at build. That is the documented fastest rollback for the admin UI,
# and it could not have worked.
#
# Keep this list in step with .gitignore: the same things are wrong to publish
# and wrong to bake in.

node_modules
.git
.gitignore

# Runtime state and secrets — mounted or supplied by compose, never copied.
data
backups
.env
.env.*
*.bak*
*.log

.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
